WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:14.575
Eliot roamed through Mickey's Sports, browsing shelves stocked with tennis rackets and baseball bats.

2
00:00:17.237 --> 00:00:22.702
His younger brother, Sean, was searching for a new goalkeeper's jersey in the soccer aisle.

3
00:00:24.164 --> 00:00:29.008
Soccer tryouts started on Monday, and Sean wanted a new jersey for good luck.

4
00:00:30.812 --> 00:00:36.355
As Eliot headed back toward the soccer gear, he spotted an athletic boy looming over Sean.

5
00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:40.097
"Sean must have bumped into a friend," he thought.

6
00:00:41.618 --> 00:00:44.379
Then he saw the kid jab Sean with a finger.

7
00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:47.761
"Hey!" Eliot shouted.

8
00:00:49.122 --> 00:00:52.824
Sean's face turned bright red when he saw Eliot rushing toward him.

9
00:00:52.844 --> 00:00:56.406
"Stay off the soccer field, loser!"

10
00:00:56.766 --> 00:00:59.608
the kid snarled before he stalked off, snickering.

11
00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:01.800
"Who was that?"

12
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:02.961
Eliot asked.

13
00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:06.662
Sean held up a lime green jersey.

14
00:01:06.682 --> 00:01:09.583
"What do you think?"

15
00:01:10.043 --> 00:01:10.983
he joked weakly.

16
00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:13.524
"Does this go with my red hair and freckles?"

17
00:01:15.505 --> 00:01:20.107
Before Eliot could reply, Sean shoved the jersey back in a pile on the shelf.

18
00:01:21.287 --> 00:01:22.107
"Let's get out of here.

19
00:01:22.547 --> 00:01:24.208
I can't afford a new jersey anyway."

20
00:01:29.764 --> 00:01:36.249
On Monday Eliot wasn't expecting to see Sean until dinnertime, after his first tryout session had ended.

21
00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:41.993
But when Eliot entered the kitchen after school, Sean was perched on a counter stool.

22
00:01:42.013 --> 00:01:45.055
"Sean! What are you doing here?"

23
00:01:45.075 --> 00:01:49.258
"I live here," he said sarcastically.

24
00:01:49.278 --> 00:01:54.902
"Remember?" "That's not what I meant," Eliot said.

25
00:01:54.922 --> 00:01:57.844
"Why aren't you at tryouts?"

26
00:01:59.308 --> 00:02:00.509
"Because I'm not trying out."

27
00:02:00.529 --> 00:02:04.371
"What?" "I won't make the team.

28
00:02:05.171 --> 00:02:05.932
So what's the point?"

29
00:02:05.952 --> 00:02:11.034
"The point is, you love soccer," Eliot said.

30
00:02:11.054 --> 00:02:15.077
"And you've been preparing for tryouts for months."

31
00:02:15.097 --> 00:02:20.540
"That was before I—" Sean's mouth abruptly snapped shut.

32
00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.661
"Before what?"

33
00:02:23.101 --> 00:02:23.981
Eliot demanded.

34
00:02:25.162 --> 00:02:28.344
Suddenly he flashed back to the scene at Mickey's Sports.

35
00:02:30.388 --> 00:02:32.209
"It's that kid from the store!

36
00:02:33.369 --> 00:02:35.289
He's the reason you skipped tryouts.

37
00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:39.711
You can't let him bully you into staying on the sidelines!"

38
00:02:39.731 --> 00:02:43.292
"It's my own fault," Sean said.

39
00:02:43.312 --> 00:02:46.893
"I shouldn't have bragged about my goalie skills to him."

40
00:02:46.913 --> 00:02:51.614
"Whoa." Eliot held up a hand.

41
00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:54.235
"It's not your fault.

42
00:02:55.615 --> 00:02:58.096
That kid is a bully, plain and simple."

43
00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:00.812
He frowned.

44
00:03:00.832 --> 00:03:03.234
"Has he harmed you physically?"

45
00:03:04.635 --> 00:03:05.715
Sean shook his head.

46
00:03:05.735 --> 00:03:08.337
"George just threatens to hurt me.

47
00:03:09.598 --> 00:03:12.419
Plus, he posts mean stuff about me on social media.

48
00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:17.062
I figured he'd finally leave me alone if I sat out tryouts this year."

49
00:03:18.803 --> 00:03:19.404
He sighed.

50
00:03:19.424 --> 00:03:22.406
"I can try out next year."

51
00:03:24.207 --> 00:03:26.208
"No way," Eliot said firmly.

52
00:03:27.604 --> 00:03:31.325
"You're not allowing some dumb bully to sabotage your soccer tryout."

53
00:03:32.265 --> 00:03:33.466
He glanced at the clock.

54
00:03:35.226 --> 00:03:36.847
"I'm driving you back to school.

55
00:03:37.967 --> 00:03:40.468
I'll give you some tips for dealing with bullies on the way."

56
00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:49.671
On Friday afternoon Eliot parked at the soccer field.

57
00:03:49.691 --> 00:03:53.972
"Today's the day," he thought anxiously.

58
00:03:55.512 --> 00:04:00.754
On the field the players huddled around Coach as she announced the names and positions of the players

59
00:04:00.794 --> 00:04:01.735
who'd made the team.

60
00:04:03.695 --> 00:04:05.556
Eliot didn't see George in the huddle.

61
00:04:08.057 --> 00:04:11.459
A few minutes later, Sean approached the car, head down.

62
00:04:11.479 --> 00:04:15.040
"Uh-oh," Eliot thought.

63
00:04:17.381 --> 00:04:19.802
Then Sean lifted his head—and grinned!

64
00:04:20.442 --> 00:04:21.823
Eliot hopped out of the car.

65
00:04:21.843 --> 00:04:24.684
"You made the team!"

66
00:04:27.572 --> 00:04:29.113
"Yep. I'm the starting goalie!"

67
00:04:29.553 --> 00:04:31.274
Sean said as Coach joined them.

68
00:04:32.715 --> 00:04:34.276
Coach shook Sean's hand.

69
00:04:34.296 --> 00:04:42.320
"Sean, you demonstrated great leadership on Monday by asking me to talk with everyone about bullying.

70
00:04:43.901 --> 00:04:46.863
It turns out you weren't the only one having issues with George."

71
00:04:48.944 --> 00:04:52.306
"Talking to an adult," Eliot thought with a smile.

72
00:04:52.326 --> 00:04:55.848
"That's a brilliant strategy for dealing with bullies.

73
00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:57.821
I wonder who thought of it."

74
00:04:58.641 --> 00:05:03.945
"Teamwork is important, and one bully can hurt the whole team," Coach went on.

75
00:05:03.965 --> 00:05:07.768
"I'm sorry I didn't know about the situation sooner.

76
00:05:09.269 --> 00:05:12.752
We now have a strict no-bullying policy, thanks to you."

77
00:05:14.153 --> 00:05:17.575
A few minutes later Eliot turned his car onto Main Street.

78
00:05:18.896 --> 00:05:19.637
"Where are we going?"

79
00:05:20.017 --> 00:05:24.160
Sean asked "Back to Mickey's Sports," he said.

80
00:05:25.409 --> 00:05:28.570
"To celebrate our victory, I'm going to buy you that green jersey!"
